    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8123" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circumactĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		circumago. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a turning around</i>,
				<i>revolving</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					9, 9, 15</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 8, §
			885</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of discourse, <i>a
				turning</i>, <i>turn</i>, <i>compass</i>, <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 20, 4</span></i>.</div>
